The patch removes the `dev_put(ifp)` call from the success path in `aoecmd_cfg_pkts()`, ensuring that the reference count is not decremented while the device is still in use. Instead, it adds the `dev_put(ifp)` call after the skb transmission in the `tx()` function, ensuring that the reference count is only decremented after the device is no longer needed, thus preventing the use-after-free condition.


